# GitHub release workflow

When the user asks to **create**, **cut**, or **publish** a release, follow this
local workflow. Do **not** add GitHub Actions; releases are built on Windows and
published with the `gh` CLI.

## Prerequisites

- [GitHub CLI](https://cli.github.com/) on PATH (`gh --version`).
- Authenticated: `gh auth login` with `repo` scope (or `GITHUB_TOKEN` for
  non-interactive runs).
- libmpv present: `npm run setup:mpv` if `src-tauri/libs/mpv/libmpv-2.dll` is
  missing.

## Steps (in order)

### 1. Build and package

```powershell
npm run release
```

This runs `tauri build` then `package:portable`, which:

- Creates an annotated tag `vMAJOR.MINOR` at HEAD (or reuses the tag already
  on HEAD).
- Writes `releases/AnimePlayer-<tag>.zip`, `releases/anime-player.exe`, and
  `releases/anime-player.exe.sha256`.

If the user already ran a recent `npm run release` and artifacts match the
intended tag, skip the rebuild after confirming with them.

`npm run release` can be slow (full Rust + frontend build). This is expected as part of the release though, so no need to warn before starting it.

### 2. Draft release notes

```powershell
npm run release:notes
```

This writes `releases/NOTES-<tag>.md` from commits since the previous tag.

### 3. Polish notes (required before publish)

Edit `releases/NOTES-<tag>.md`:

- Rewrite commit subjects into user-facing bullets (fixes, features, UI).
- Drop checkpoint/noise commits and merge-only lines.
- Group related changes.

Show the polished draft to the user (or save it) before publishing unless they
explicitly asked you to publish without review.

### 4. Publish to GitHub

```powershell
npm run release:publish
```

Optional flags (pass through to the script):

- `--notes <path>` — notes file (default: `releases/NOTES-<tag>.md`)
- `--tag <vX.Y>` — override tag

The script verifies `gh` auth, required artifacts, and
`releases/.build-meta.json` (commit/tag must match HEAD and the publish tag),
creates the tag if needed, runs `git push origin <tag>`, then `gh release create`
with the zip, exe, and sha256 attached.

## Git / safety

- **Do not** `git push origin main` (or any branch) unless the user explicitly
  asks. `release:publish` only pushes the release tag.
- After publish, remind the user to push `main` if release commits are not on
  the remote yet.
- If publish fails because the release already exists: `gh release view <tag>`
  and only delete/recreate with user approval.

## End-user updater alignment

GitHub release assets must include exactly what `_update.ps1` expects:

- `anime-player.exe`
- `anime-player.exe.sha256` (uppercase hex, `hash anime-player.exe` format)

The portable zip must include `update.bat`, `_update.ps1`, `libmpv-2.dll`, and
`VERSION.txt` (handled by `package-portable.mjs`).

